The latching current of a Silicon Controlled Rectifier (SCR) is always greater than its holding current, as a higher current is needed to establish conduction during turn-on than to maintain it in steady state. Typically, the latching current is approximately 2 to 3 times the magnitude of the holding current. Therefore, for a latching current of 20 mA, the most appropriate value for the holding current is 10 mA.

